    "title": "One dead from shooting near midtown Charlotte shopping center: CMPD - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Doug Coats No media credit provided. ,\n2 hours ago\nCHARLOTTE, N.C. (QUEEN CITY NEWS) — The victim from the shooting in midtown Charlotte Wednesday night is dead.\nCharlotte-Mecklenburg Police say the shooting occurred just before 8 pm. in the 900 block of Metropolitan Avenue, near Target. Officers located a victim with gunshot wounds who was transported to a local hospital, but later died from their injuries.\nCMPD is investigating the shooting as a homicide. No suspects have been named at this time,.\nCMPD detectives, Crime Scene Search and Operations Command were assisted by Charlotte Fire Department and Medic.\nIf anyone has information on the incident, they are asked to call Charlotte Crime Stoppers at 704-334-1600, use the P3 Tips mobile app or visit the Crime Stoppers website.\nThis is a Developing Story . Check back for updates\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Queen City News.",
